## Claude Platform opens native OpenTelemetry agent tracing in public beta

Source: Anthropic — https://claude.com/resources/articles/agent-observability-on-the-claude-platform
Published: 2026-10-14
Channel: news

Anthropic announced OpenTelemetry tracing for Claude Managed Agents, the Messages API, and Claude SDKs in public beta. The export covers agent turns, model calls, and tool activity, with latency, token usage, and identifying fields. Traces follow the OpenTelemetry GenAI semantic conventions and can go to tools accepting a standard OTLP endpoint. Managed Agents and Messages API users configure a destination in the Claude Console; the announcement describes automatic export for Claude SDKs. This brings platform agent execution into existing investigation and evaluation workflows.

For operators, the useful question is whether a trace explains a real failure across application and agent boundaries. Our editorial recommendation is to exercise one model call, one tool failure, and one MCP interaction, then inspect parentage, identifiers, and arrival at the destination. Check content handling before using sensitive traffic. Treat the beta announcement as an integration capability, not measured proof of complete coverage or correct agent behavior. Customer improvement figures in the article are testimonials, not a benchmark of the export itself.

Why it matters: Verify trace arrival and correlation with a known failing agent run.

