## Langfuse shares LLM credentials across projects with local overrides

Source: Langfuse · Tobias Wochinger — https://langfuse.com/changelog/2026-10-14-organization-llm-connections
Published: 2026-10-14
Channel: news

Langfuse added organization-level LLM connections that are automatically available to projects within the organization. These connections supply centrally managed credentials for the Playground, evaluations, and experiments. A project can use different credentials by creating a connection with the same name; the project connection takes precedence. Organization owners and administrators manage shared connections in the interface. Public API management with an organization-scoped key is also available on Enterprise Cloud and self-hosted Enterprise Edition. The announcement describes connection configuration, without claiming equivalent evaluator behavior across providers.

The operational benefit is less repeated setup, but central configuration also creates a shared dependency for evaluation jobs. Our editorial recommendation is to test credential rotation against a small experiment, then confirm which connection each project resolves. Include a project with an intentional override so a centrally changed key does not obscure local routing. Record the model and rubric with results when comparing experiments. Shared credentials simplify administration; reproducible evaluations still require evidence of the actual model configuration used for each run.

Why it matters: Test credential resolution and rotation before relying on shared evaluation connections.

